Subject: [PATCH 0093] flight recorder: a VFS context of the writing thread for each open

Wildcat Lake test 40 (0092): shutdown got past the unmount wait, then panicked in namei under the flight writer's
vnode_open (zone_require_ro failed, addr 0, from get_bsdthreadtask_info): the context made at start belonged to the
attach thread, which had exited. Each drain now makes a context of its own thread for the open and releases it.

diff --git a/gpu-port/xkpi/xnu/nmx_flight.cpp b/gpu-port/xkpi/xnu/nmx_flight.cpp
index 575e475..cca827f 100644
--- a/gpu-port/xkpi/xnu/nmx_flight.cpp
+++ b/gpu-port/xkpi/xnu/nmx_flight.cpp
@@ -351,8 +351,20 @@ static void flight_drain_locked(void)
     ring_unlock(st0);
     if (empty)
         return;
+    /*
+     * A context of this thread for each open: the one made at start belonged to the attach thread, long gone, and a
+     * reopen with it panicked in namei during shutdown (zone_require_ro on its thread's task, test 40).
+     */
+    vfs_context_t start_ctx = gCtx;
+    gCtx = vfs_context_create(nullptr);
+    if (gCtx == nullptr) {
+        gCtx = start_ctx;
+        return;
+    }
     if (vnode_open(kFlightPath, FWRITE | O_NOFOLLOW, 0644, 0, &gVp, gCtx) != 0) {
         gVp = nullptr;
+        vfs_context_rele(gCtx);
+        gCtx = start_ctx;
         return;     /* e.g. the volume is being unmounted: the ring keeps the lines */
     }
     for (int pass = 0; pass < 32; pass++) {
@@ -380,6 +392,8 @@ static void flight_drain_locked(void)
     VNOP_FSYNC(gVp, MNT_WAIT, gCtx);
     vnode_close(gVp, FWRITE, gCtx);
     gVp = nullptr;
+    vfs_context_rele(gCtx);
+    gCtx = start_ctx;
 }
 
 /* called by the attach once the root file system is up; the ring holds everything printed since the kext loaded */
